From 5f54cc88edab2e90ebe983c41f9d140110c630eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:09:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 43/47] Flipping items without a board: use the standard layer
 pairs (backport of master 6a26ce9d)

Saving a back-side footprint to a library (fp upgrade of a legacy .mod, for
example) flips it to the front while it has no parent board, and
PCB_TEXT::Flip() and friends called GetBoard()->FlipLayer() on nullptr
(ASan: SEGV in BOARD::FlipLayer). Add BOARD_ITEM::GetFlippedLayer(), which
falls back to ::FlipLayer() like FOOTPRINT::Flip() already did, and use it
for the items a footprint can hold. master fixed this in 6a26ce9d
("pcbnew: BOARD-is-null cleanup"); the 10.0 branch has not.

Found by tools/bughunt (fp upgrade of legacy .mod libraries).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
